      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-4z5o-cross-instance-figure-urls/cat-harness.jsonld#skill/sub-kg-lifecycle",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Skill",
      "name": "sub-kg-lifecycle",
      "title": "Sub-KG lifecycle — staged here, separated later",
      "description": "A sub-KG is a knowledge graph staged as a directory inside a harnessed repository, declared as its own instance, that may later leave for a repository of its own. The lifecycle: declare it in place, grow it, stage it for separation (one import seam, the separation guard, a self-contained rehearsal), and then, each behind an explicit owner confirmation, create the repository, copy the staged contents in with history, re-point the declaration, verify on a fresh clone and delete the in-repo copy. Extracted in retrospect from the staged IG separations of 2026-09-21 to 2026-10-06 (beans n3ni, rbz3, kg83, hcpz). The light sibling of kg-separation: use this for a DATA instance that leaves whole, and kg-separation when a graph must split into a content repository and a tools repository.",
      "inPackage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-4z5o-cross-instance-figure-urls/cat-harness.jsonld#package/graph-management"
