      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-4z5o-cross-instance-figure-urls/cat-harness.jsonld#actor/deep-researcher",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Actor",
      "localId": "deep-researcher",
      "actorKind": "agent",
      "title": "Deep researcher",
      "description": "Answers a question from the corpus this folio ALREADY HOLDS, and stands behind the answer's citations. `agent` rather than `person`, and the reason is the opposite of `librarian`'s: nothing in this loop decides what may be redistributed or what a source means in law — it plans, retrieves, filters and synthesises over material a person has already admitted. The role admits `person` too, and no person-shaped actor is registered for it because none has been named; inventing one would assert a party this repository does not have. WHAT THIS ACTOR MAY NOT DO is report an agent's draft figure description as what the figure shows — `schemas/narrative.ts` holds that line, and it is why an agent performing this is legitimate in the first place. ITS PERMISSION IS IN THE ODRL POLICY, not here: #1186 moved every actor's own `permissions` list into `policies/folio-defaults.jsonld` as an assignee/action rule, and `odrl.test.ts` fails any actor file that still carries one. This actor was written with a `permissions` list about two hours before that landed; the grant itself is unchanged — `content-authoring`, stated once, in the policy.",
      "meta": {
        "workflow": "folio-assistant-core/processes/library/deep-document-research.bpmn#Lane_DeepResearcher"
      },
      "hasCapability": [],
      "mayTakeRole": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-4z5o-cross-instance-figure-urls/cat-harness.jsonld#role/deep-researcher"
      ],
      "permissionName": [
        "content-authoring"
      ],
      "alternateOf": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#actor/deep-researcher"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-4z5o-cross-instance-figure-urls/cat-harness.jsonld#actor/platform-boundary-guard",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Actor",
      "localId": "platform-boundary-guard",
      "actorKind": "agent",
      "title": "Platform boundary guard",
      "description": "Keeps folio-specific content out of platform code and platform code out of folios. Reads a change and judges whether a literal names one folio, whether a new content type needs an adapter or only a profile, and whether a node declares what it is. Its findings are advice: it does not accept a change into the corpus, which is the editor's lane. Acts as `code-reviewer` — the question it asks is whether the NODE is sound, which a passing test suite does not answer.",
