    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/STAGING/claude-4z5o-cross-instance-figure-urls/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_Review",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Process",
      "name": "Review task",
      "summary": "The generic review position: classify what changed, descend into the review that fits it, consolidate what comes back, and accept or send back.",
      "description": "The generic review position: classify what changed, descend into the review that fits it, consolidate what comes back, and accept or send back.\n\nYou are in this process for any change under review. It is a DISPATCHER — the actor takes on the inner lane's role for the call path only — which is why prose and code can both be reviewed without either reviewer having to know the other's criteria. A change that is both — prose and the code it describes — takes a branch of its own, which reviews the two against each other; the gateway is exclusive and takes exactly one branch, so the earlier wording, that such a change goes through both, described a route the diagram could not take (issue #1042).\n\nThe accept-or-send-back decision lives here and nowhere beneath it. The subprocesses produce findings; this is the only lane entitled to turn findings into an outcome, and keeping that single makes \"who decided\" answerable.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/content/review-task.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/blob/main/cat-harness/processes/content/review-task.bpmn",
