      "title": "JSON-LD prefix check",
      "description": "Check every committed JSON-LD document in both directions: each prefix a context binds is spoken by something (or forward-declared with a reason), each prefix a document SPEAKS as a key or `@type` is bound in its context, each binding onto one of our own namespaces is spelt as that instance's stub, and every plain key in a document on the published content context is a declared term (never descending into an `@json` value). A context it cannot resolve is reported as undetermined, never clean.",
