      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/0.1.0/ns#Role",
      "prefLabel": "Deep researcher",
      "title": "Deep researcher",
      "notation": "deep-researcher",
      "description": "Answers a question FROM a corpus already held, and is answerable for the answer. Distinct from `librarian`, which decides what to capture, and from `ingestion-agent`, which derives structure from what was captured: both produce the corpus, and this role consumes it. Added 2026-09-23 with the `doc-researcher` methodology, because the accountability it names — somebody who must stand behind a synthesis and its citations — belonged to no declared role. THE LANE IT BINDS IS DRAWN IN ANOTHER INSTANCE — the `Deep researcher` lane of `folio-assistant-core/processes/library/deep-document-research.bpmn`, which names this role with `<folio:role ref>`. It carried a `lanes[]` here for about an hour on 2026-09-23 before #1168 landed and inverted the relation: a lane names its role, and a role does not list its lanes, because a general node never names its users. The binding is therefore stated once, on the lane, and this role says nothing about where it is drawn.",
      "sourceKind": "role-registry",
      "actorKinds": [
        "person",
        "agent"
      ],
