      "notation": "session-record",
      "description": "A session's context — who is acting, which instances are open, what it waits on. A MECHANICAL role and an `actedUpon` one: written to as the session moves and read by a sibling deciding whether a claim is live, and it decides nothing. Modelled on `work-plan`, `corpus` and `log`, the stores that are acted upon rather than acting. It carries `session-context` because the shape of what is written IS the discipline here — unlike `work-plan`, whose store has a CLI, this one is written by a machine that may be an LLM playing the part, so the schema is the contract.",
